// name :
"P1630807727" "The Origin of Power"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3358022767" "Origins Path"
// DetailString :
"P2992413834" "You found her, <color deepskyblue>Ashley McKnight</color>, standing outside the University. She said she wanted you to learn about the origin of power. She said you looked like you were smarter than your average crook. She said a lot of things.<br><br>You went and talked with <color deepskyblue>Virgil Tarikoss</color> regarding the origins of magic. Once you got past his ego, a hard task for even someone as powerful as yourself, you learned that <color orange>magic was created from strife and that mankind holds a power greater than even the gods.</color> What this means for you here and now, you're unsure. Perhaps speaking with the other people Ashley wishes you to talk to would clear this up."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - Cap_McKnight_Arc_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P2144718763" "You look at one of the ancient tablets that you 'forgot' to return to Ashley McKnight and are reminded of the events you've come to know as...<br><br><color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br>Ashley McKnight sent you all over Cap Au Diable to talk to different villains. Each villain was from a different origin. You talked to Tarikoss about magic, Marshall Brass regarding his natural skill and training and the Golden Roller about technology. You even spoke with Dr. Shelly Percey about her experiments on humans and with Dr. Dmitri Krylov regarding the creation of the mutant origin during the late thirties.<br><br>All of this showed you the history of origins... of powers. However, it wasn't until the Circle of Thorns decided to try and corrupt that power that you got to take action. They had found an ancient cave filled with tablets. These tablets were said to hold the secrets of power and the Thorns were attempting to bend that power to their own end, taking it away from you. <br><br>Thankfully, you don't mind getting a little dirty. You went through that cave and made sure no one, not even Ashley McKnight, would be able to use those tablets to their advantage. No one except you, of course."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OriginMagic 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1056969827" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>You dare interrupt me? You are either bold or stupid. Which is it?"
// Answer Text :
"P804009185" "Bold"
// Answer Text :
"P2500187764" "Stupid"
// Page BoldPage Text :
"P1096973367" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Ah! Really? Perhaps you are.<br><br>I know why you are here. Ashley McKnight has been sending many of you here to speak with me regarding the origins of magic. Well, listen closely."
// Answer Text :
"P3364067830" "Learn about magic"
// Page StupidPage Text :
"P3950694395" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I can not tell if you are serious or simply seeing how far you can push me. Let me warn you... Oh, stupid one, do not push Tarikoss.<br><br>Now, I know why you're here, even if someone as dim as you has forgotten. You wish to learn about the origin of magic. I will explain it to you, but I make no guarantees you will comprehend any of it."
// Page OriginPage1 Text :
"P2793070206" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Magic is the child of two parents, War and Hatred. Spawned from the gods themselves, magic rages out of control across the realms like a spoiled child greedily devouring all in its wake.<br><br>Man however, is the one true disciple. Only we are able to command magic, bending it to do our bidding. With that control, we become gods ourselves."
// Answer Text :
"P1433069963" "I would like to hear more"
// Answer Text :
"P2963146842" "I'm bored"
// Page OriginPage2 Text :
"P3628183244" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I'm sure even one such as you is aware of the Circle of Thorns. Fools believe that they were once a peaceful, happy group that sat around in their ivory towers contemplating their navels. In fact, the real Circle of Thorns commanded the very demons from the dark realms. These demons were the slaves to the Circle and for thousands or years, the Circle fought across the globe and even into other realms. Once again, mankind proved its power over the gods and once again, even the gods attempted to stop them. <color deepskyblue>Ermeeth</color>, the god of the Circle did not like how his children were using their power so he teamed up with another god, named <color deepskyblue>Hequat</color>. The two of them attempted to control the ways of magic and man. They would have failed, of course, if not for the revolt of the demons against the Circle of Thorns. The demons rose up against their masters just as the gods descended upon them. The battle that raged broke the world, shattering all of the power across mankind. The demons retreated into their caves and the gods returned to their mountains and man was left to pick up the pieces.<br><br>Magic as we know it now is a shadow of what it once was. The power that we once commanded was omnipotent. Now, it is little more than parlor tricks.<br><br>Now be gone. I am done with you."
// Answer Text :
"P945842507" "Be gone"
// Page NotOriginPage Text :
"P3205933443" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I do not expect one such as you to understand magic. That would be like trying to explain sight to the blind. So, I will keep the lesson a simple one.<br><br>Magic was created from strife. It's power was such that even the gods could not wield it properly. However, man is so much more than the gods and we commanded magic as the true masters that we are. However, there was a war against the gods and the demons and man. The power thrown around during this war broke the world and, in its breaking, the power of magic was nearly wiped out. What we now know of magic is nothing more than a shadow of what it once was.<br><br>Leave me, you have made me dwell on topics best left forgotten... for now."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page FinalPage Text :
"P2916081068" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>If you do not care to listen, I do not care to explain. I should have known you would not understand the significance of this.<br><br>Be gone."
// Page Fallback Text :
"P2629565143" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I really don't want to talk to you right now. You should move along and get back to fighting something."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2909898712" "You might not want to hear this, but there is more to your abilities than a simple twist of fate. You're connected to something bigger than you or I. It's the one thing that ties all of us together, not just in the Rogue Isle and Paragon City, but all of us, through all time. It's <color deepskyblue>the Origin of Power</color>. Where it comes from, how it changes and what it means to us now.<br><br>It's true, this is a history lesson of sorts, but it's also an instruction manual. This task is not full of combat and near death experiences. So, if that's what you're after, perhaps it's best you go elsewhere and steal something or mug someone.<br><br>If you are interested, perhaps you'll learn something."
// AcceptString :
"P228072557" "Take a history lesson"
// SendOffString :
"P573889446" "Well done. I thought I saw more depth in those eyes than just a dumb thug. But, I digress.<br><br>So, your first lesson is to speak with a mystic here in Cap au Diable. His name is <color deepskyblue>Tarikoss</color>. He should be able to guide you through the ways of Magic."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P541270051" "Talk to Tarikoss"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P566174989" "Go and talk with <color deepskyblue>Tarikoss</color> regarding the origin of Magic. If he's willing, his talk should be very enlightening."
// TaskTitle :
"P705000025" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1373655451" "Hello, {HeroName}. Yes, it is true and hopefully obvious, that I am a man of magic."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2078845874" "Virgil Tarikoss is not a man who wastes time, or words. I doubt you got much out of him, even if you are of magic origin.<br><br>However, I hope what you did get was at least enlightening regarding his view of where magic comes from."
// RandomFameString :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OriginNaturalDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P590260868" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>{Hero}, I do not know if this is the best time for me to be seen with you. Something is going on in this city and it's making everyone nervous.<br><br>Be quick about it. What intel do you seek?"
// Answer Text :
"P1977292035" "Ask about being a villain without powers"
// Page OriginPage1 Text :
"P3328319335" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Yes, it's true, both you and I have no powers per se. But I've trained all my life to get to where I am. I feel as if I've pushed myself so far past what others would think of as our peak, that it makes myself question where human ends and where superhuman begins.<br><br>I'm sure you understand what I'm talking about. For as long as I can remember I've always known that only the strong survive in the ring. It doesn't matter if the ring is an old Roman gladiator pit or Cap Au Diable. It's all the same. We fight or we die."
// Answer Text :
"P1419602472" "Thank you"
// Page NotOriginPage Text :
"P700325172" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Look at you standing here asking me how I got to where I was without powers. Are you trying to pity me?<br><br>I'll have you know that I've taken out half a dozen villains with more power than you before I showed up to work today. Do you know how I, a lowly human, can do that while the rest of you fly around this city like you're gods? I can take you down because I'm just that much better than you. Take away your powers and you're nothing. Nothing! I win because I want it more than you. I win because I will never give up.<br><br>Now, get out of my face, I don't have time for this."
// Page Fallback Text :
"P155691542" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I don't have time for this. Go back to Ashley and deal with her. I'm working here."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2556079327" "There's a guy here who is in charge of all Arachnos military operations in Cap Au Diable. His name is Marshal Brass. He got to his place in the world with no powers or technology of any kind. He's a natural. I'd like you to talk to him about what sets him apart from other men."
// AcceptString :
"P2558420184" "Talk to Marshal Brass"
// SendOffString :
"P1245701258" "Marshal Brass is a man I have yet to figure out. He works for Arachnos, yet I believe he is a good man. My father would tell me I'm just partial to a man in a uniform, perhaps."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4218556103" "Please go talk to Marshal Brass about being a natural.<br><br>And if you happen to get his cell number I wouldn't turn it down."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1438488940" ""Hello, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P949007463" "What did you learn from Brass? Really? Huh, I would have expected him to be more forthcoming. I wonder if he's hiding something."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OriginTech 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1307860250" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>My associates tell me you're investigating the origins. Interesting... There any money in it for me? Didn't think so.<br><br>Well, what can I do for you in the thirty seconds I'm giving you to waste my time?"
// Answer Text :
"P2907924721" "Ask about technology"
// Page OriginPage1 Text :
"P3236002718" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Technology, as I've always thought of it, is our intellect given form. You can tell a lot about a person by what they create. Take King Midas for example, a man who can turn anything he touches to gold, yet he's still a thief.<br><br>But technology is so much more than that. It's about pushing boundaries, scientifically, morally and socially. Today's thief is tomorrow's hero.<br><br>Have you ever heard the story of Daedalus?"
// Answer Text :
"P2623709885" "No. What is it?"
// Answer Text :
"P517359712" "Not interested."
// Page OriginPage2 Text :
"P1622754758" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Daedalus was a guy back in ancient Rome who was commanded to build a maze for King Minos. Inside this labyrinth, Minos hid his half-son because he was embarrassed by the monstrosity his wife had birthed. That monstrosity was the Minotaur.<br><br>As if this wasn't bad enough, the king would send in slaves, convicts and anyone else he didn't like, into the maze for the Minotaur to eat. Once you entered the maze you never came back.<br><br>Well, King Minos had a daughter who was in love with some poor fool and the King was going to throw him into the maze. The daughter went to Daedalus and begged him to help her - to help her lover find a way out of the maze.<br><br>Daedalus agreed to help. What he gave her was a ball of string and told her to have him tie it to a branch on his way inside. As long as he had the string he would be able to find his way out.<br><br>Nice story. Do you understand the point of it?"
// Answer Text :
"P3513136317" "Not interested"
// Page OriginPage3 Text :
"P721219802" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>The point is that technology is merely a tool of what we are. It can be used for either good or evil. In and of itself it is literally a moral.<br><br>By the way, your thirty seconds are up."
// Answer Text :
"P118975244" "Thanks"
// Page NotOriginPage Text :
"P3549183294" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Technology, as I've always thought of it, is our intellect given form. You can tell a lot about a person by what they create. Take King Midas for example, a man who can turn anything he touches to gold, yet he's still a thief.<br><br>But technology is so much more than that. It's about pushing boundaries, scientifically, morally and socially. Today's thief is tomorrow's hero.<br><br>I know I said I was going to give you thirty seconds, but I have some other boundaries that need pushing. Shove off."
// Page FinalPage Text :
"P790385051" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>See you soon, {Hero}."
// Page Fallback Text :
"P308885783" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I don't have time for this. Go back to Ashley McKnight and deal with her. I'm working here."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1519514458" "You should get a kick out of this one. I was trying to find a technology contact you could talk to and the only one I came up with was Golden Roller. I hear he's been linked to the Gold Brickers and Lord Midas as well.<br><br>You up for a little chat?"
// AcceptString :
"P2753928812" "Talk to the Golden Roller"
// SendOffString :
"P387617131" "Odds are he'll try and scam you, but just get in and get any information you can and get out."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3158713293" "Head over to Golden Roller and see what he has to say about the technology origin. I personally can't wait to hear what he's going to talk about."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1127431811" "Hello, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4250285501" "Like I said, the Golden Roller is an interesting character. I hope you learned something useful from him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OriginScience 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P504102163" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Hello, {HeroName}. I have seen many things in my 'research' on the metahuman population. The one thing that I have noticed more than any other is the adaptive nature of the human body. Where other species would simply curl up and die after being bombarded by countless rays of radiation, the human body adapts and overcomes. It's really very beautiful."
// Answer Text :
"P2585986144" "Tell me more"
// Page OriginPage1 Text :
"P3347307698" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Ah, you are really a nice piece of work.<br><br>Who did it to you? It's really wonderful, I like the balance of your form and your power. Make sure you thank the person for me. I really appreciate good work.<br><br>So, what can I help you with... ah, Ashley sent you over here to talk about science and its origins. Let me ask you a question first, are you familiar with the Rikti?"
// Answer Text :
"P2678157141" "No, tell me about them"
// Answer Text :
"P2819814666" "Yes, why?"
// Page OriginPage2 Text :
"P2039929686" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>You know the Rikti look upon science in the same way we do. They see it as a means to bettering themselves. They've gone so far as to actually genetically modify themselves. I'm not sure how long they've been doing that, but I'd guess it's been for some time.<br><br>I can't say when we first started looking at science to better ourselves. I spend so much time looking forward, I never saw a point in looking back.<br><br>That's one thing you have to learn with science, if you stop to ask yourself if you should do something, you've already lost faith in thinking that you can do it. Morality is simply an excuse for the unintelligent masses. I have never believed in it ... only science."
// Page NotOriginPage Text :
"P2238581443" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>The one thing you have to learn with science is that if you stop to ask yourself if you should do something, you've already lost faith in thinking that you can do it.<br><br>Morality is simply an excuse for the unintelligent masses. They dress themselves up in falsity to justify their own lack of imagination and ability. It's sad, really.<br><br>Well, I've got work to do, and regretfully, it's not on you. I hope you got the answers you were looking for. If you ever want to step into my lab, I'd love to have a look at your DNA."
// Page FinalPage Text :
"P2779847455" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I hope you got the answers you were looking for. If you ever want to step into my lab, I'd love to have a look at your DNA."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3361725048" "Dr. Shelly Percey is known for her research and testing of meta humans. I would say she's an expert when it comes to the origin of science only because she's likely created a few herself.<br><br>She, above all else in Cap, could tell you about the science origin."
// AcceptString :
"P3320338847" "Talk to Dr. Shelly Percey"
// SendOffString :
"P3527663824" "Dr. Percey's research has caused her to work with many of the groups here in Cap, including Dr. Aeon himself. However, I don't believe the two of them are very close."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3577821581" "Go talk to Dr. Shelly Percey. She will explain to you about the origin of science."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3061735684" "Dr. Shelly Percey is an interesting woman and by interesting I mean creepy. I hope she didn't invite you into her lab. She tried that with me once. I think she still has a scar from where I jabbed the syringe into her neck.<br><br>But I'm on a tangent... I'm glad you talked to her. I hope she gave you some useful information."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - OriginMutant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3422861943" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>Hello, {HeroName}. Mutants are not people born differently. They are simply... NOT human. This mutation, as the layman calls it, is not an old occurrence. My research shows no record of a mutant before 1938? Interesting, nyet?"
// Page OriginPage1 Text :
"P2788585198" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>In 1938, the first atom was split. This changed how all atoms acted within our reality. Everything changed.<br><br>However, I believe that there are many mutants that are misclassified. In fact, in my research I have discovered many sub-types of mutants that perhaps were their own origin at one point. This leads me to believe that the path of origins is an ever changing one. Interesting, nyet?"
// Page NotOriginPage Text :
"P1998225567" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>You, obviously, are not a mutant. I, obviously, am not a mutant. That building over there, is obviously not a mutant. Do you understand? Da, I knew you would see my point. Mutants are not like us and the building. I think, in fact, that mutants are not like mutants... ah, now that is something.<br><br>I must get back to work. I hope you got the answers you were looking for. Give Ashley McKnight my regards. I remember her father well... Too well."
// Page FinalPage Text :
"P3333253974" "<color deepskyblue>The Origin of Power</color><br><br>I hope you got the answers you were looking for. Give Ashley McKnight my regards. I remember her father well... Too well."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1038253436" "You should really go talk to Dmitri Krylov. He's an expert in Mutants. Granted, I think he got that way from performing a number of experiments on them."
// AcceptString :
"P1837056678" "Talk to Dmitri Krylov"
// SendOffString :
"P3882065671" "Dmitri would know better than anyone else the history of Mutants. If you get the chance, ask him if he knows my father. That should give you a good laugh."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3944873761" "You really need to go talk to Dmitri. He knows a lot about Mutants."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1926061400" "As I said, Dmitri knows a lot about mutants... What? He asked about my father? Not surprising, since my father chased him halfway across the globe a number of years back. He never told me what it was about, but I can only guess it had to do with Dmitri's experiments."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1639245118" "So, I hoped we'd be able to avoid this, but it doesn't look like it. While you were off talking to the different people about their origins, the Circle of Thorns have gotten wind of what's going on. They're up to something and I'm going to need your help to stop it."
// AcceptString :
"P875528548" "Help stop what's going on with the Circle"
// SendOffString :
"P1120374641" "They've unearthed some old relics and are beginning to ask the same questions we are regarding powers and their origin. Honestly, this scares the snot out of me because if these guys can get a handle on where powers come from and how to control them, then the world will be in a bad place. <br><br>Please, get in there and stop them. I know this isn't your sort of thing, but what they're doing affects all of us, hero or villain."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P287363933" "Stop Circle of Thorns"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1659923407" "I still need you to get into that nearby cave and get those relics they've unearthed. Without those relics, they won't be able to rewrite how villains use their powers."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1224468182" "<color deepskyblue>Finale</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P651369381" "The Circle of Thorns are attempting to uncover the mysteries behind powers. If that happens, there's no telling what they will do with that knowledge."

